# Object is NOT read-only: extending it is a documented urbiscript
# idiom, so `Object.foo = 5` succeeds and the value round-trips.  The
# companion claim — that Lobby is read-only — is lobby_readonly.chk.

## mode: repl

> {"id":11,"op":"eval","code":"Object.foo = 5; Object.foo"}
< "id":11 | "kind":"result" | "value":"5"
< "id":11 | "kind":"done"
